# C4-5 (round 19, writer 10): L4_2_load_schedule with the day 0, an inline figure (L §7.1), in place of the row dom:
# load sees the schedule (L §8.3 item 9: literals and keys of a declared index), and no month has a day 0, so the
# schedule gives no date in the run: LOAD-SCHEDULE. The old comment:
# L §4.2: "A schedule that gives no date in the run is refused at load (LOAD-SCHEDULE)": day 31 of February 2026
# alone gives none at every key of the move.  (A schedule outside a move's on is not checked: what its run is isn't
# stated, HANDOVER.md.)
=== m.tally
model sch
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
index qm = month 2026-02..2026-02
input dom: int
input amt: money PLN
input cal: calendar

move pay[m in qm]: transfers
  on schedule(m, 0, unadjusted, cal)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 31
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q1: count(x in transfers over 2026), flows(pay, 2026)
ask q2: x.day for x in transfers over 2026
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SCHEDULE schedule schedule(m, 0, unadjusted, cal) (the day of pay) gives no date in the run (m.tally:16)
